o asserts abort, and I reproduced glibc's exact `__assert_fail` format using the original C expression text and line numbers, with `program_invocation_short_name` and a `build.rs`-resolved `__FILE__`.\n\n## Differential testing\n\nA `dlopen`-based driver exercised both libraries side by side, one case per process (the library corrupts its own heap by design), comparing **stdout, stderr and exit status**: table dumps, `convert_pix` across bpp `{-1,0..5}` × 7 dimension sets, all four input alignments, exact/short/oversized output buffers, stored/fixed/dynamic/RLE/Huffman-only streams up to 400 KB multi-block, hand-built error-path streams, table tampering, and 2001 mutated/truncated/random fuzz inputs.\n\n**PASS=2046 FAIL=0** — byte-identical throughout, including 50+ cases where both abort with `SIGABRT` at the same assertion with the same diagnostic, and cases where both trigger the same glibc heap-corruption abort.\n\n`cargo build --release` is clean (0 warnings) from scratch; `c_src/` is unmodified (0 files touched) and all scratch build/test artifacts were removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":113987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bfb4734-56d9-4687-8189-51db6f2bf72a","uuid":"d6865b80-3409-4175-8462-f98a9e64ce20","timestamp":"2026-08-27T07:26:23.075Z"}
